# .gitignore template for a LangQuest exercise repository.
# Copy this to the root of your exercise repo (rename to `.gitignore`).

# Machine-bound identity attestation — specific to each machine and regenerated
# on that machine's first online launch. NEVER commit it.
.lq.attest

# NOTE: do NOT ignore `.lq.progress`.
# It holds your encrypted, GitHub-account-bound progress. Committing it is how
# you sync progress across your machines (home PC, school laptop, …):
#
#   git add .lq.progress && git commit -m "progress" && git push   # after a session
#   git pull                                                        # before the next
#
# It is encrypted and account-bound, so it is safe to commit even in a public
# fork — nobody else can read your scores or reuse the file. Because it is a
# binary blob git cannot merge two versions, so always pull before and push
# after a session if you use more than one machine.

# Compiled test binaries / build artifacts produced while verifying exercises.
*.o
*.out
a.out
target/
__pycache__/
